// A contract's identity is (namespace, name). `int32` conforms to `markx::Marker`; this bound is on
// `marky::Marker`, a different contract that happens to share the bare name — and share a method name too,
// so nothing downstream would catch the mistake.
//
// Conformances used to be pre-scanned under the BARE contract name, so the two were conflated and this
// compiled. It then produced a wrong-but-plausible program: the call resolved to markx's `mark`.
import { markx::Marker, marky::needsMarker };

fn int32 main() {
    int32 x = 5;
    return needsMarker(v: ref x);
}
